# Dash on the test course: the example conversation for docs/WRITING.md, added without code. It shows a condition,
# a choice, a flag set and a second visit. Placeholder lines, not the Pier's.

~ start
[if dash_met] => again
Dash [grin]: You're the new one. Nim, right? Vesper's latest project.
Nim: I'm not a project.
Dash: Everyone's a project. I was a project. Now I'm the fastest thing in the Old Quarter.
- Prove it. => race
- Good for you. => shrug

~ race
Dash [grin]: Gate to the end of the lane. Loser buys.
set dash_race_offered
set dash_met
=> END

~ shrug
Dash: Wow. Cold. I like it.
set dash_met
=> END

~ again
[if dash_race_offered] Dash: The race is still on. I'll even give you a head start. A small one.
[if not dash_race_offered] Dash: Back again? Changed your mind about the race?
